{"name":"Golden Pheasant","hex":"#cf9632","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden pheasant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful game bird originating from China, of species Chrysolophus pictus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_pheasant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden pheasant","blocks":[{"text":"The golden pheasant, also known as the Chinese pheasant, and rainbow pheasant, is a gamebird of the order Galliformes and the family Phasianidae (pheasants). The genus name is from Ancient Greek khrusolophos, \"with golden crest\", and pictus is Latin for \"painted\" from pingere, \"to paint\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Fasanhona-1.jpg/330px-Fasanhona-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_pheasant","wikidata":"Q335113"},{"title":"Pheasant","blocks":[{"text":"Pheasants are birds of several genera within the family Phasianidae in the order Galliformes. Although they can be found all over the world in introduced populations, the pheasant genera's native range is restricted to Eurasia. The classification \"pheasant\" is paraphyletic, as birds referred to as pheasants are included within both the subfamilies Phasianinae and Pavoninae, and in many cases are more closely related to smaller phasianids, grouse, and turkey than to other pheasants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Pheasant.jpg/330px-Pheasant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pheasant","wikidata":"Q214169"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https: